 "text": "So here's a story most people have never heard. Back in the 1950s, a researcher named Jerry Morris started looking at London's double-decker buses. Same buses. Same routes. But two very different jobs. You had the driver, who sat all day... and the conductor, who was up and down those stairs collecting tickets. And the drivers? They had more heart disease. Sudden heart-related deaths were about twice as common. That one study helped kick off the whole science of exercise and heart health.",
